Z||000004||gabriel||02-27-2001||10:46 PM||||  <BR>   I've looked at this feature, & it is apparently the way it was designed. To my knowledge, all Fiero windows stop there.  They even manufacture a special tool so that you can remove the dew wipe screws, since you can't fit a regular screwdriver on them.<P>  If you look at it, you will see what I mean.<P>  Since I also dislike limitations, I'm going to look at this in more depth.<P>  I'll be taking apart another door in a week or two, so I'll look at it, however, I suspect that the window size vis a vis roof height & door size is a limiting factor here.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||02-28-2001||07:54 AM||||I think the only way you're going to be able to make them travel down further is to lengthen the "scissors" mechanism that raises and lowers the window.  If you did this, they would also travel up more.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
